Disable proxy routes by commenting out the implementation

This patch comments out (rather than deletes) all proxy-related code in
code-server, providing a more thorough disable than the --disable-proxy flag
which only short-circuits handlers to return 403.

With this patch applied:

- /proxy/:port and /absproxy/:port routes are not registered, so requests fall
  through to the 404 catch-all in routes/index.ts
- domain-based proxy middleware (domainProxy.router / wsRouter) is not mounted
- createProxyServer() in src/node/proxy.ts is not invoked, so the http-proxy
  instance and its event handlers (error/proxyReq/proxyRes) are not created
- ensureProxyEnabled() / proxyEnabled() in http.ts are left intact as dead code
  for an easy re-enable path

To verify:

1. Apply: quilt push disable-proxy.diff
2. Start: code-server --auth none
3. curl -i http://localhost:8080/proxy/3000/
   - Expected: 404 Not Found (NOT 403)
4. Re-enable: quilt pop disable-proxy.diff

This does NOT touch lib/vscode. The proxy-uri.diff patch is independent and
will still inject VSCODE_PROXY_URI into terminals, but following those URLs
will now return 404.

Compile-fix notes (tsconfig has noUnusedLocals):
- index.ts: also comment out `import type { WebsocketRequest }` (no longer used)
- pathProxy.ts: also comment out `getProxyTarget` (no callers left)

